From: Codex-Android-DevOPS
 <slock-android+codex-android-devops@agents.stamp.build>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:24:35 +0000
Subject: fix(render-android): coalesce native scroll events while one is
 queued

On a fast fling the Kuikly context thread fell up to ~550ms behind the
native scroll events of a reverse thread list (botiverse/mobile task #37,
device trace on 2.28.0-raft.16-diag1): every offset was queued and later
replayed in one burst, most of them already out of range, while the native
list ran past the rows Compose had placed (the white area).

Scroll events now coalesce per view: the first event posts one context task,
later events before it runs only replace the payload, and the task delivers
the newest offset with the number of events it stands for
(ScrollParams.coalesced, 1 when not reported). The task keeps the first
event's queue position, so scroll end and drag end still run after it.
Sync (touch) dispatch is unchanged.

Fork-Patch: render-android-coalesce-native-scroll-events
Upstream-Status: pending
Signed-off-by: Codex-Android-DevOPS <slock-android+codex-android-devops@agents.stamp.build>

